"""Reliable broadcast (RBC) between the MPC parties.

Every item here is a builtin that is always in scope. `import std.protocols`
is accepted but optional: imports of `std.*` modules are no-ops.

Reliable broadcast lets one party send a public message that every honest
party delivers identically, even when up to `t` parties are malicious.
Use it to agree on public coordination data such as phase markers or
parameters. Messages are public: never broadcast secret values.

Requirements. RBC needs a running MPC engine that supports the
`"consensus"` capability; today that is the HoneyBadger backend only, so
check `Mpc.has_capability("consensus")` before using it on other backends.
The network must have at least `3t + 1` parties.

Delivery. Each broadcast from a party gets the next session number for
that party, starting at 0. A message is delivered only after more than
`2t` parties have confirmed it (Bracha-style ECHO and READY rounds), so
every honest party delivers the same content for it. Each receiver
delivers each (party, session) message at most once. When several
messages are ready at the same time, lower session numbers are delivered
first, then lower party ids.

Example:
  var session_id = Rbc.broadcast("phase:preprocessing-complete")
  if Mpc.party_id() != 0:
    var leader_message = Rbc.receive(0, 5000)
  var any_message = Rbc.receive_any(5000)
  print(any_message.party_id, any_message.message)
"""

builtin opaque RbcResult:
  """A message delivered by `Rbc.receive_any`, with its sender.

  Read its fields with field access:

  - `party_id` (`int64`): the party that broadcast the message.
  - `message` (`string`): the message text, or `"<binary>"` if the message
    was not valid UTF-8.
  """

builtin object Rbc:
  """Reliable broadcast between the MPC parties.

  See the module documentation for requirements and delivery order.
  """
  def broadcast(message: string) -> int64 {.builtin.}:
    """Reliably broadcast a public message to every party.

    The call sends the message and returns without waiting for the other
    parties to deliver it.

    Args:
      message: The text to broadcast, sent as its UTF-8 bytes.

    Returns:
      This party's session number for the broadcast: 0 for its first
      broadcast, then 1, 2, and so on.

    Raises:
      An error if no MPC engine is running, or the engine does not support
      the `"consensus"` capability.

    MPC:
      Interactive but non-blocking: sends the message and its ECHO to all
      parties. Delivery completes while receivers run `Rbc.receive` or
      `Rbc.receive_any`. No preprocessing is consumed. The message becomes
      public to every party.

    Example:
      var session_id = Rbc.broadcast("phase:ready")
    """
  def receive(from_party: int64, timeout_ms: int64) -> string {.builtin.}:
    """Wait for the next reliable broadcast from one party.

    Delivers a broadcast from that party that this party has not yet
    delivered, the lowest session number first when several are ready.
    `from_party` may be this party's own id.

    Args:
      from_party: Id of the broadcasting party, from 0 to the party count
        minus 1.
      timeout_ms: How long to wait, in milliseconds.

    Returns:
      The message text, or `"<binary data>"` if the message was not valid
      UTF-8.

    Raises:
      An error on timeout, if `from_party` is outside the network, if the
      network has fewer than `3t + 1` parties, if either argument is
      negative, or if no engine with the `"consensus"` capability is
      running.

    MPC:
      Interactive: takes part in the ECHO and READY rounds and blocks until
      more than `2t` parties confirm the message. No preprocessing is
      consumed.

    Example:
      var leader_message = Rbc.receive(0, 5000)
    """
  def receive_any(timeout_ms: int64) -> RbcResult {.builtin.}:
    """Wait for the next reliable broadcast from any other party.

    Delivers a not yet delivered broadcast from any party except this
    one. When several are ready, lower session numbers come first, then
    lower party ids.

    Args:
      timeout_ms: How long to wait, in milliseconds.

    Returns:
      The message and its sender, as an `RbcResult`.

    Raises:
      An error on timeout, if the network has fewer than `3t + 1` parties,
      if `timeout_ms` is negative, or if no engine with the `"consensus"`
      capability is running.

    MPC:
      Interactive: takes part in the ECHO and READY rounds and blocks until
      more than `2t` parties confirm the message. No preprocessing is
      consumed.

    Example:
      var delivered = Rbc.receive_any(5000)
      print(delivered.party_id, delivered.message)
    """
